  "kanji": "久",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 久\ntitle: a long time\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-5, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 3\nradical: 丿\nradicalNumber: 4\nonyomi: [キュウ, ク]\nkunyomi: [ひさ.しい]\ndistractors: [夕, 欠, 友]\n---\n\n# 久 — a long time\n\n**Strokes:** 3 · **Key (radical):** 丿 (no. 4) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n久 points to a long stretch of time. 久しい ひさしい describes a long time having passed, while 久しぶり ひさしぶり describes doing or encountering something after a long interval.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Picture a person leaning back for a very long wait, with one stroke stretching out to the right.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| キュウ | on | [永久](../words/永久.md) えいきゅう - permanence; eternity |\n| ク | on | 久遠 くおん - eternity; the remote past or future (Buddhist terminology) |\n| ひさ.しい | kun | 久しい ひさしい - long (time that has passed); old (story) |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [久しぶり](../words/久しぶり.md) ひさしぶり - after a long time\n- [永久](../words/永久.md) えいきゅう - permanence; eternity\n- 久しい ひさしい - long in elapsed time\n\n## Notes\n\n- 久しぶり is not a statement that an activity itself lasts a long time: 久しぶりに会う ひさしぶりにあう means meet after a long interval.\n- Distinguish 久 from [夕](夕.md) ゆう, evening: 久's final stroke extends to the lower right.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1227340, 1227370, 1576520, 1577900.\n\nUsage evidence: [Seisenban Nihon Kokugo Daijiten: 久遠](https://kotobank.jp/word/%E4%B9%85%E9%81%A0-476617).\n",
